// 05 - Encoding: certutil -encode
// Source   : rewritten after the challenge from the commands in report/incident-report.md,
//            to show how this stage can be surfaced. Uses only the columns confirmed
//            in my original query (TimeGenerated, DeviceName, ProcessCommandLine).
// Finds    : the zip being Base64-encoded to win_update_kb5034.b64 before exfiltration.
// Library  : kql-detection-library/detections/defense-evasion/certutil-encode-decode.kql
// Lab scope: LOG(N) Pacific Silent Corridor training scenario; all values are synthetic.
SilentCorridorX_CL
| where ProcessCommandLine has "certutil" and ProcessCommandLine has "-encode"
| project TimeGenerated, DeviceName, ProcessCommandLine
